From: magos <local>
Date: Sat, 28 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Scale Steel plugin decorations linearly

LOCAL PATCH - OURS, NOT FOR UPSTREAM. See README.md in this directory.

The Steel decoration API added by 0001-0005 pushes one annotation layer per
overlay (a `Layer` binds one highlight to the whole layer) and clones the
document's entire inlay-hints snapshot on every add-overlay! /
add-styled-inlay-hint / add-line-background! call. Both are quadratic in the
number of plugin overlays: the plugin pass is O(N^2), and
TextAnnotations::overlay_at looks every rendered grapheme up against all N
layers.

Fix: keep all plugin overlays in one document-owned, char-sorted layer that
carries a per-entry highlight, and grow the snapshot in place through
Document::inlay_hints_mut.

Measured on ~/.claude/plans/auth-seam-implementation.md (91KB, 1502 lines, 58
table rows => 28,587 plugin overlays per render pass), CPU consumed by one
cursor move while vista renders (100 jiffies = 1s CPU):

    without this patch   166 jiffies (1.66 s)
    with this patch        4 jiffies (40 ms)
    vista not rendering    1 jiffy   (unpatched-helix baseline)

TextAnnotation build per rendered frame with this patch: 87 us median, 436 us
max. Rendered output is byte-identical with and without this patch (captured
terminal output of a table-heavy buffer), and buffer contents are unaffected:
conceals stay display-only.
